{
 "elemod": 2,
 "id": "digiseq",
 "version": "0.2",
 "title": "DIGISEQ",
 "description": "DIGISEQ for the Digitone mk1: sequencer types a track plays in place of its own trigs, chosen per track on TRIG's second page (TYPE: OFF, SNAKE or 185). SNAKE: a Cartesian sequencer after MDD Snake (and Make Noise's Rene), eight cells in a 4 x 2 grid walked by a path (DIGISNAKE 1.3; its projects load as they were). 185: a stage sequencer after ML-185 (and RYK's M-185): eight stages, each with a pitch, a velocity, a length of 1-8 clock pulses and a mode (OFF, ONE, ALL every DIV pulses, HOLD for the whole stage), with DIR, STAGES, CLOCK (1/8 .. 2X), SCALE, RANGE, note LEN and SHIFT. Hold TRIG + YES randomises a page, FUNC + YES the note pages, TRIG + NO and FUNC + NO reload, TRIG + REC / STOP copy and paste, TRIG + PLAY clears, TRIG + UP / DOWN changes TYPE, TRIG + FUNC + REC prints into the track. Saved with the project; on OS 1.44 kept over a power cycle. Needs core-dn1 3.3 and seq-events 0.2 (ev_fire_len). Not with DIGISNAKE, which it replaces.",
 "category": "Sequencer",
 "author": "Robbie",
 "license": "GPL-2.0-or-later",
 "target": {
  "device": "digitone-mk1",
  "product": "Digitone mk1",
  "os": "1.43",
  "syx_sha256": "c5a54cc05b921f2e4bd814834c5365c2a5aa01d7772a9a2961fac1c3095bf9aa",
  "section3_sha256": "3831a477a2a22befb23c42e47e782853da49566ef5d0a1767fcf6c30e6767414",
  "section3_len": 2732208
 },
